---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="FAQ - CloudDroid" description="Frequently asked questions about CloudDroid cloud Android workspaces, pricing, and features.">
  <div class="bg-slate-light py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate">Everything you need to know about CloudDroid. Can't find the answer? <a href="mailto:support@clouddroid.eu" class="text-navy underline">Contact support</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-4">
        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            What Android versions are supported?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">We support Android 10 through Android 14. Each instance runs a clean, isolated Android environment with full ADB access. You can select the Android version when creating a new instance.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            How does data isolation work?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">Each instance runs in a strictly containerized environment with zero cross-talk between customers. Data is encrypted at rest with AES-256 and transmitted over TLS 1.3. Instances are destroyed upon deletion.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            Can I access my instance via ADB?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">Yes. All plans include ADB access over a secure tunnel. You can connect your local ADB client to your instance for debugging, automation, and app installation.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            What regions are available?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">We currently operate in EU (Frankfurt) and US (Virginia) regions. You can select your preferred region during instance creation. Additional regions are planned based on demand.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            How do I extend my access?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">Access is granted per purchase. When your access period is about to end, simply purchase your plan again to extend it. Your existing account and data will be preserved.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            Do you offer a free trial?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">We do not offer a free trial. However, we provide a 14-day money-back guarantee if you are not satisfied with the service. Contact support@clouddroid.eu within 14 days of purchase for a full refund.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            What payment methods do you accept?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">We accept all major credit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express) via Dodo Payments. European customers can also pay via iDEAL, Bancontact, and other local methods through Mollie.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            Is there a setup fee?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">No. There are no setup fees or hidden charges. You pay only the one-time access fee listed on our pricing page.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            How do I integrate with CI/CD?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
           <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">Professional and Team plans include CI/CD support. You can trigger instance provisioning, run tests, and collect results via our REST API or webhooks. See our <a href="/api-docs" class="text-navy underline">API documentation</a> for details.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            What happens if I exceed my storage limit?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">If you exceed your storage limit, you will receive a warning notification. You can either upgrade your plan or delete unused data. Instances are not immediately suspended, but sustained overages may result in reduced performance.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            Do you offer custom enterprise plans?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">Yes. Contact us at sales@clouddroid.eu for custom pricing, dedicated infrastructure, SLA guarantees, and priority support tailored to your organization's needs.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>